   "source": [
    "# Project: Human or Machine?- Fase 2 (CP4)\n",
    "**Team name:** [Team 7 - RAKDBR]\n",
    "**Description:** Official evaluation, performance analysis, and interface testing notebook using the baseline model (TF-IDF + Logistic Regression)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "45cb0769-702c-47a7-80cb-a8caf7bf44a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 4: Model Evaluation and Comparison\n",
    "In this section, the performance of the classification model—based on **TF-IDF and Logistic Regression**—is evaluated using the test set (`test.tsv`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Performance Metrics Obtained:\n",
    "* **Accuracy:** 0.5991 (59.91%)\n",
    "* **F1-Score (Weighted average):** 0.5039 (50.39%)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Analysis of the Confusion Matrix and Metrics:\n",
    "The model exhibits a significant bias toward the positive class (labeled as AI, class 1), achieving a very high recall for that class (0.97), while showing limited performance for the class representing human-written texts (class 0, with a recall of 0.13). This demonstrates that simple statistical features based on word frequencies struggle to capture the diversity of human language."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "36364d75-f74a-4355-aea6-3c7d77e6b01c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 5: Error Analysis Cases (5 Cases)\n",
    "The following are five practical scenarios in which the model exhibits failures or specific behaviors when interacting with the interface:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Language Barrier (False Positive):** When text in Spanish is entered, the model tends to misclassify it as AI-generated, as its training vocabulary is dominated by the English language.\n",
    "2. **Colloquial Language and Idioms:** Informal expressions or everyday slang allow the baseline model to correctly identify human-written text, as these patterns of informal natural language are not typically replicated by generative models.\n",
    "3. **Sensitivity to Short Texts:** Extremely brief sentences (e.g., \"Ok\" or \"Yes\") lack sufficient TF-IDF frequency features for the classifier to produce a reliable prediction.\n",
    "4. **Formal/Academic Style (False Negative):** Paragraphs written by humans that feature a highly formal and technical structure are mistaken for AI-generated content.\n",
    "5. **Presence of Spelling Errors:** Spelling mistakes or imperfect punctuation disrupt the predictable structure that generative models emulate, helping the baseline model categorize such text as human-written."
   ]
  }
 ],
